# Release Packaging

## Firefox

```powershell
cd d:\proj\4changal
$v = (Get-Content manifest.json | ConvertFrom-Json).version
$files = @("manifest.json","main.js","labelsModule.js","settingsModule.js","background.js","util.js","styles.css","options.html","jquery.js","icon.png","README.md")
Compress-Archive -Path $files -DestinationPath "gallery-wg-$v.zip" -Force
```

Upload at: https://addons.mozilla.org/developers/addon/4chan-gallery-mode-wg/versions

## Chrome

First sync shared files, then package:

```powershell
Copy-Item -Path main.js,labelsModule.js,settingsModule.js,util.js,styles.css -Destination chrome\ -Force
cd chrome
$v = (Get-Content manifest.json | ConvertFrom-Json).version
$files = @("manifest.json","browser-polyfill.js","background.js","main.js","labelsModule.js","settingsModule.js","util.js","styles.css","options.html","jquery.js","icon.png","README.md")
Compress-Archive -Path $files -DestinationPath "..\gallery-wg-chrome-$v.zip" -Force
```

Upload at: Chrome Web Store Developer Dashboard.

## Chrome-specific files (do NOT overwrite from Firefox)

- `chrome/manifest.json` — service_worker, optional_host_permissions, browser-polyfill in content_scripts
- `chrome/background.js` — uses chrome.* directly (no polyfill in service workers)
- `chrome/browser-polyfill.js` — maps browser.* → chrome.* for content scripts
- `chrome/options.html` — uses bundled jquery.js, not CDN
